"Let $P$ be an $n\\times n$ partial Latin square in which each symbol, row, and column contains at most $\\frac{1}{4}n$ nonblank cells. **Daykin–Häggkvist conjecture.** Every such partial Latin square can be completed to a Latin square. This is a central completion problem for partial Latin squares and is linked to Nash-Williams's conjecture on triangle decompositions; the source does not provide evidence of resolution."